        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Bit Generations: Digidrive is a Game Boy Advance video game released in 2006 by Q-Games and Nintendo. Of all of the bit Generations games, this is the only one not developed by skip Ltd.\n\nGameplay\nThe game's menu has three options, including Play (the game's main mode), Demo (watch a computer play the game), and Download (give demo to another player). Play is the game's primary mode, and it includes:\n\nSingle: The game's single player mode.\nVs. Computer: Play against a computer.\nVs. 2 player: Play same game as above, though with a friend.\nCredits: Available after unlocking. Shows who made the game.\nThe single player mode features a variety of other options you can choose from as well, though Start is the main one.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "2006",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
